  "worked_solution": "We model the number of insects using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=2H.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nH(t)={H}_{0}\\,{e}^{2t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${H}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $120$ insects in the habitat, so we have ${H}_{0}=120.$\n\nTherefore, the number of insects $H$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nH(t)=120\\,{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of insects when $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H(2) & =120\\,{e}^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =120\\,{e}^{4} \\\\  & \u22486551.78\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of insects after $2$ months is approximately $6552$ insects.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
